        "comments": "The assembly drAlcAlpi1.hap1.1 is based on 102x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species shows a high chromosome number and different chromosome distribution patterns. In addition, it has a many rearrangements and hybridisation events history, reasons why It was not possible to infer ploidy. The karyotype may vary within the species, depending on the location the specimen was collected. The haplotypes could not be separated during curation, so the complete set of chromosomes was submitted. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on Chromosome 48 from 5.84 to 6.83, Chromosome 62 from 9.40 to 10.89, Chromosome 73 from 10.0 to 11.19, Chromosome 96 from 4.95 to 6.14 and Chromosome 149 from 4.06 to 5.44 Mbp are uncertain.",
